# Commercial S12.1 server-context review diagnosis

- Scope: final pre-freeze review against the documented canonical server state.
- Findings: the freeze helper lacked repository-scoped `safe.directory`; backup
  required an attached branch; and preflight did not reject the known
  long-lived `tu1nz_sync_all.sh --loop` competing Control mutator.
- Corrections:
  - every freeze-helper Git command uses scoped `safe.directory`;
  - backup records attached versus detached state and rollback restores and
    verifies the exact commit/tree and attachment posture;
  - read-only preflight stops before backup with
    `WAITING_OPERATOR_CONFLICTING_CONTROL_SYNC` when the exact sync loop exists.
- No global Git exception, process termination, gate bypass, runtime attempt,
  provider expansion, or secret exposure is introduced.
- Rollback: restore the prior reviewed Control commit; no server mutation has
  occurred.
